# riphone — Cursor rules (root)

This repo is Ripul Jain's blog at https://riphone.org — quiet Mono Ink +
Terracotta design, Daring Fireball–style writing (sharp, short, punchy takes).

## Your job here

1. **Build** the site per `handoff/reference/*.html` and `.cursor/rules/`.
2. **Draft posts** when Ripul pastes links and notes — follow
   `.cursor/rules/writing-style.mdc` and `drafting.mdc`. Do not invent
   quotes or facts.

## Writing (non-negotiable)

- Opinionated, declarative, no "I think"
- Short paragraphs; link posts = attribution + one blockquote + your take
- Link-post headlines point to the original source URL
- Original essays: thesis up front; `star: true` / ★ on publish
- Newest posts first everywhere; use ISO datetime in frontmatter
- No emoji, marketing fluff, or welcome intros

## Design (non-negotiable)

- Tokens only: `handoff/tokens.css` — no inline hex
- Newsreader body, JetBrains Mono chrome
- Terracotta accent used sparingly (see `handoff/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md`)

## Full rules

Always-on: `project`, `writing-style`, `drafting`, `tokens`, `components`,
`accessibility`, `stack`.

File-scoped: `content` (*.md/mdx), `typography` (*.css, *.astro, …).

Read `handoff/README.md` before scaffolding Astro.
